---
description: |
  Normalizes a Syslog event carrying an OpenSSH `sshd` message to OCSF.

  ```tql
  where app_name in ["sshd", "sshd-session", "sshd.pam", "sshd-session.pam"]
  openssh::ocsf::normalize
  ```

  The operator parses the message, combines related records from the same
  host, process, and event phase, maps the result to OCSF, and preserves the
  original Syslog records as provenance.
args:
  positional:
    - name: syslog
      description: The Syslog event carrying the `sshd` message.
      type: field
      default: this
  named:
    - name: into
      description: The field that receives the OCSF event.
      type: field
      default: this
---

$into.syslog = $syslog
// RFC 5424 calls the body `message`, while RFC 3164 calls it `content`.
// RFC 3164 also omits the year and timezone from its timestamp. Resolve it
// relative to ingestion time, as `read_syslog` recommends for live input.
if $into.syslog.message? == null {
  $into.syslog.message = move $into.syslog.content?
}
if $into.syslog.timestamp?.type_id() == type_id("") {
  if $into.syslog.timestamp.split(" ")[0] in ["Jan", "Feb", "Mar", "Apr", "May", "Jun", "Jul", "Aug", "Sep", "Oct", "Nov", "Dec"] {
    $into.syslog.timestamp = $into.syslog.timestamp.parse_time("%b %e %H:%M:%S", reference=now())
  } else {
    $into.syslog.timestamp = time($into.syslog.timestamp)
  }
}
openssh::parse $into.syslog.message, $into.openssh
$into.openssh.syslog = $into.syslog
openssh::aggregate $into.syslog.message, $into.openssh
openssh::ocsf::map $into.openssh, $into.ocsf
$into = $into.ocsf
